As an additional note, while installing xcode worked for me, it only works when you install from the command line after downloading the source from cran.  So the sequence goes :

1. Install xcode (or just the gcc toolchain)
2. Download desired packages (here plyr, but iterators, gridExtra, ... have the same problems)
3. Install them from the terminal

Then they will work fine.  If you try to reinstall from inside R with install.packages, you have to repeat 3.  Why doesn't the install work from inside R?

Thanks!
david.

