Simon,

Yes, you are correct it was a fresh install of xcode from the app store (4.2 Build 4D199) on OS 10.7.2. Before I formatted I had previously installed 4.1 on the machine. When I formatted and reinstalled everything I panicked because I needed a functioning R install with some newer packages. I trawled for almost 2 hours trying to find a solution before finding a suggestion on a linux forum that linking gcc could fix it (inappropriately, thanks for the correction).

During my adventures I went here:
http://cran.r-project.org/bin/macosx/RMacOSX-FAQ.html#What-is-needed-to-build-R
 and read...
Recent installations feature Xcode Tools folder containing the necessary installer. If neither of the above works for you, download Xcode from http://developer.apple.com/tools/xcode/.

The link takes you to the App store download for Lion. I see no where to download 4.1 and the tools <http://r.research.att.com/tools/> page seems to assume that you can get your hands on it.  I no longer have any OSX disc...

Sounds like the best bet is to install gcc-4.2? From where?

 Brandon

P.S. I know enough to be dangerous (clearly), but not enough to know what I'm doing most of the time.

